# CodeOnTheGo Project Rules

## Project Overview
This is a React Native/Expo app with a Node.js backend that uses:
- Supabase for database and authentication
- Google Gemini AI for code analysis and lesson generation
- Express.js for the backend API

## Backend Structure
- `backend/src/index.js` - Main server file with API endpoints
- `backend/src/services/` - Service files for database operations
- `backend/.env` - Environment variables (GEMINI_API_KEY, SUPABASE_URL, etc.)

## Key Endpoints
- `/api/analyze` - Code analysis with Gemini AI
- `/generate-lesson` - Generate educational content
- `/generate-quiz` - Generate quiz questions
- `/api/quiz-completion` - Save quiz results

## Database Tables (Supabase)
- `user_problem_progress` - User progress on problems
- `user_lesson_completion` - Lesson and quiz completion
- `user_profiles` - User skill levels and profiles
- `topics` - Available topics
- `problems` - LeetCode problems

## Common Issues
- Backend server not starting (port conflicts, missing dependencies)
- AI endpoints returning 404 (duplicate routes, missing environment variables)
- Database connection issues (wrong Supabase credentials)

## MCP Configuration
Use Supabase MCP to:
- Query database tables directly
- Check user progress and lesson completion
- Verify data integrity
- Debug authentication issues 